+/* VPULL=1 (opt-in): GPU vertex pulling for indexed TRIANGLES, strips and fans
+ * (rsx_vpull.h). Instead of converting every distinct vertex into a 256-byte
+ * slot (read_vp_vertex_fast), the guest bytes of the vertices a FIFO index
+ * batch spans are copied into a byte ring, and the batch's indices -- strips
+ * and fans turned into list indices exactly as upload_strip_vp_ix does --
+ * are rebased onto that copy. The vertex shader decodes the attributes.
+ * Records whose attributes are not one plain interleaved stream (frequency
+ * divider, different strides or memories, attributes far apart, VF_FAST other
+ * than 2), a very sparse first batch, a full ring or index buffer, and every
+ * other primitive keep the CPU path. With VPULL unset nothing here runs: same
+ * root signature, buffers, shaders and draws. A [VPULL] line every 5 s. */
